.TH GWG 1 "August 2026" "gwg 0.2.6.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gwg \- initialize and administer a WireGuard server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gwg
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gwg
creates and maintains WireGuard server and peer configuration. Installing the
Debian package does not create a service account or initialize a server.
Administrative commands are run through sudo. Initialization is an explicit
administrative operation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Prepare system directories, enable IPv4 forwarding and initialize a default
wg0 server. This command must be run as root.
.TP
.BI "server install --name " interface " --network " prefix " --port " port
Create and start a WireGuard server with explicit parameters.
.TP
.BI "server show"
Display WireGuard interface and peer state.
.TP
.BI "server stat"
Display per-peer transfer counters.
.TP
.BI "user add " user
Add a peer and generate its client configuration.
.TP
.BI "user remove " user
Remove a peer.
.TP
.BI "user block " user
Disable a peer without deleting its configuration.
.TP
.BI "user unblock " user
Enable a blocked peer.
.TP
.B user list
Display configured peers.
.TP
.BI "template show " "server|client"
Display the current WireGuard configuration template.
.TP
.BI "template set " "server|client" " --file " path
Replace a configuration template with the contents of a file.
.TP
.BI "template reset " "server|client"
Restore the built-in configuration template.
.TP
.B tc
Manage traffic-control classes, filters and service state.
.TP
.B version
Display gwg and Go versions.
.SH INITIALIZATION
Install the package and its dependencies with APT, then initialize explicitly:
.PP
.nf
sudo apt install ./gwg_VERSION_ARCH.deb
sudo gwg init
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard
WireGuard and gwg configuration files.
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/.wg_manager/templates
Editable server and client WireGuard configuration templates.
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/90-gwg.conf
IPv4 forwarding setting created by
.BR "gwg init" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wg (8),
.BR wg-quick (8),
.BR tc (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
